WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:09.820
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life
retreat, online retreat, kind of cool

00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:17.250
right? And I'm very pleased to have Zhou
Xiaoping, Alison, helping me to translate.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:27.410
Thank you for coming and again thank you
and Stanley

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:34.920
for helping me for so many years. I'm very
grateful. So,

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.260
we're on... this is going to be online

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:49.400
session number two, segment two, and today
we're going to do a meditation together.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:59.090
There's a special way to prepare for a
meditation. In Tibetan, it's called yenlak dunpa (YAN

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:11.279
LAG BDUN PA), and these are seven different
steps to prepare properly for a

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:21.229
meditation. And I know a lot of you have
heard them before; and of course I've

00:01:21.229 --> 00:01:31.779
been teaching them for ten years during
these lam rim (LAM RIM) teachings, but my hope is

00:01:31.779 --> 00:01:45.700
that ... and by the way I'd like thank the
ACI Executive Director, Tim Lowenhaupt,

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:54.709
and I'm very grateful that he's really
organized this online retreat among all

00:01:54.709 --> 00:02:02.009
the other things he does. And I was kind
of excited to do the retreat because I

00:02:02.009 --> 00:02:07.079
think many more people will be able to
enjoy that they don't have to travel

00:02:07.079 --> 00:02:17.040
somewhere and spend a lot of money;

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:21.060
so I feel like a lot of people who
haven't been able to come to the lam rim

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:34.239
retreats in the last ten years will be
able to attend this one. So, I think

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:43.290
it's good for all of us if we can just
review these preliminaries to a

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:56.580
meditation. And so I apologize if you
heard these seven steps before, but I

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:05.760
think they're extremely important and I
myself do them almost every day. I like

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:13.200
to say that you can't run a
race in the Olympics

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:26.549
if you don't warm up first. And I think
it's easier to warm up your body than it

00:03:26.549 --> 00:03:41.659
is to warm up your mind. When I was young
and I was first learning to drive a car—

00:03:41.659 --> 00:03:49.780
which Allison promised to learn this
year—I remember the

00:03:49.780 --> 00:04:02.670
first thing the teacher told us: when you
get in your car, start the car, and then

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:08.159
wait for three, four, or five minutes.

00:04:08.159 --> 00:04:17.060
Don't drive it right away, because a car
needs time to warm up. And he said your

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:26.970
car will last twice as long if you warm
up.

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:40.650
And the last used car I had
when I lived here, it was almost 30 years

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:54.550
old and it lasted fine for 30 years. In
fact, it's still running; I gave it to my

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:58.850
friend. So, that's a big piece of
knowledge for anyone:

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:14.560
warm up your car. Just for five minutes.
There's a there's a hot and cold

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:24.770
needle [guage] in your car. It goes like this.
So wait until the needle goes off of cold.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:29.400
And meditation is

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:39.590
the same. So, I've been meditating for, I
don't know, over 40 years and I still

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:51.940
cannot start a meditation cold. Even
after over 40 years of meditating I

00:05:51.940 --> 00:06:03.879
need to warm up my meditation mind
before I start meditating. And that

00:06:03.879 --> 00:06:11.949
warm-up has become a very enjoyable and
precious part of my life.

00:06:11.949 --> 00:06:22.039
So actually in the morning, I look
forward to having coffee and meditation

00:06:22.039 --> 00:06:34.610
warm up. So, we're going to do the warm up
together, and then I'm going to teach you

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:48.910
other kinds of meditations, sort of
warm-ups. And in my opinion, all of

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:56.569
your meditations, every day you could choose
one of these three warm-ups

00:06:56.569 --> 00:07:14.220
to put in your meditation. The first warm-up,
which is called the seven-part warm-up, its

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:27.289
focus is one of the teachers in your
life. And the theory behind that warm-up

00:07:27.289 --> 00:07:33.960
is called sak jang (BSAGS SBYANG).
So sak (BSAGS) means: just before you do your

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:48.290
main meditation, try to collect some real
quick good karma. And jang (SBYANG) means: just

00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:58.259
before you start your main meditation
try to clean some bad seeds out of your

00:07:58.259 --> 00:07:59.520
mind.

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:09.319
And right now it's spring
in Arizona where I'm talking, this is the

00:08:09.319 --> 00:08:18.300
actual week that we are planting most of
our garden.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:28.979
First we do the jang, we get rid of all
the old dirty leaves and old problems in

00:08:28.979 --> 00:08:43.010
the soil. We clean the soil. When you're
preparing for a meditation, it's very

00:08:43.010 --> 00:08:53.910
very sweet to clean any bad seeds you
made in the last 24 hours.

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:59.700
So, don't try to think of all the bad
seeds you did in your life, you will

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:14.070
never start your meditation. It's very
powerful and it's enough to just think

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:26.250
about the main bad seeds you might have
planted in the last 24 hours.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:40.430
Then you do the sak part. 
Sak means "make some instant good karma." 
So, jang—SBYANG is

00:09:40.430 --> 00:09:50.160
like cleaning out the soil; making it
clean for the new plant. And then sak is

00:09:50.160 --> 00:10:02.150
kind of like, "put fertilizer and some
water on the plant", and the plant is your

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:03.720
meditation.

00:10:03.720 --> 00:10:10.570
Now, the easiest way to clean away your
bad seeds; the easiest way to plant some

00:10:10.570 --> 00:10:20.520
new good seeds, is to invite one of the
teachers in your life to meditate with

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:33.620
you. So, these seven steps for preparing
for meditation, they're all based on one

00:10:33.620 --> 00:10:48.080
of your teachers. Later in this series of
25 videos, I'll teach you a special way

00:10:48.080 --> 00:11:00.590
to prepare for your meditation which is
more based on shamatha; and shamatha

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:13.100
means, "making your mind very very
peaceful so you can see emptiness." So,

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:19.270
sometimes we'll do this seven steps

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:25.740
focused on one of our teachers, but
sometimes the preparation for a

00:11:25.740 --> 00:11:38.060
meditation this month will be a
traditional preparation for shamatha

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:48.810
meditation, which is making the mind
quiet enough to see emptiness. And then

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:57.250
we'll have a third kind of meditation
warm-up, and that will be based on

00:11:57.250 --> 00:12:05.830
emptiness itself. So, three kinds of
warm-up, and today we're going to do the

00:12:05.830 --> 00:12:11.500
seven-step warm-up together.

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:22.380
And it's based on our teacher. We'll be
choosing one of the teachers in our life.

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:27.160
Of course the most powerful example
would be your heart teacher, if you have

00:12:27.160 --> 00:12:39.190
a heart teacher. The short definition of a
heart teacher is: "the teacher who

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:48.910
helped you the most in this life". So, you
can use ... that would be the most common

00:12:48.910 --> 00:12:58.330
example of a teacher to use for this
meditation, but you could use other teachers

00:12:58.330 --> 00:13:11.860
in your life. Your dad and your mom were
your first great teachers. And then

00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:16.560
obviously in your school life,

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:18.690
everyone met a few special teachers in

00:13:18.690 --> 00:13:29.360
their life. Sometimes it's not a school
teacher, sometimes it's a sport teacher,

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:38.950
or an art teacher, or a music teacher.

00:13:38.950 --> 00:13:49.750
Later on you met someone who taught you
how to do your occupation, your job.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:56.450
That's a special teacher in our life. If
you're married, then your wife or husband

00:13:56.450 --> 00:14:07.780
is a great teacher in your life. If you
have children, those are great teachers.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:18.370
Even in your middle age, your parents who
are elderly are nice teachers to have in

00:14:18.370 --> 00:14:21.750
your life.

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:29.940
If you don't have a heart teacher,
you can also just imagine one, and you could

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:42.060
bring that teacher to prepare for these
seven steps of meditation. And of course

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:45.310
you could take your historical teachers.

00:14:45.310 --> 00:15:05.010
It could be Buddha, Jesus, Moses Confucius,
Lao Tzu—many, many choices. Now, just in

00:15:05.010 --> 00:15:12.140
the last few weeks my personal favorite
has been Nagarjuna ...

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:24.330
Arya Nagarjuna. So, I've been doing the
seven steps with him. And then every

00:15:24.330 --> 00:15:27.200
three weeks or so, you can
change the teacher, or every day if you

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:41.410
want. So, the picture we used to introduce
this segment shows a monk walking

00:15:41.410 --> 00:15:53.410
down a country road, and I've
visited many times the place where

00:15:53.410 --> 00:16:04.440
Nagarjuna is supposed to have been born
and studied.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:14.830
In Tibetan, it's called bet tey yul (BEE DA'I YUL),
kind of like "the land of the coconuts." So,

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:22.630
I always imagined when I when I think of
Nagarjuna ... I don't like to close my eyes

00:16:22.630 --> 00:16:34.040
and think of a painting or a statue; I
like to think of Nagarjuna

00:16:34.040 --> 00:16:44.510
walking down the road to his house. He's
just like a real person. Somehow I

00:16:44.510 --> 00:17:00.450
imagine he's a very kind of funny person,
and extremely intelligent, and extremely

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:07.610
moral, and a great understanding of
emptiness. That's why sometimes he's

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:22.889
called "The Arya." So, let's start our seven steps.

00:17:22.889 --> 00:17:24.889
If you don't know how to prepare your

00:17:24.889 --> 00:17:36.220
meditation space, or the correct posture;
I taught it in the first two years of

00:17:36.220 --> 00:17:48.990
the ten years, and I suggest you go check
it on The Knowledge Base. I'll ask Tim to

00:17:48.990 --> 00:17:56.880
put the link up for you

00:17:56.880 --> 00:18:05.519
at the end of this video. Okay, so let's
get ready to meditate. The main thing is

00:18:05.519 --> 00:18:16.320
to be comfortable. The most comfortable
place in my house is my couch, and I

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:25.039
meditate on the couch and it's just very
comfortable to me. So, sit somewhere where

00:18:25.039 --> 00:18:35.009
you don't have to move, and sit up
straight. It's always good to put some

00:18:35.009 --> 00:18:49.909
cushions to raise the back of your
pigu (屁股), bottom. Your hands are comfortable

00:18:49.909 --> 00:19:04.210
on your legs. Any way that's comfortable
for you. Sometimes I will put a small

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:17.419
cushion in my lap, and I like to rest
my hands there. Most important is that your

00:19:17.419 --> 00:19:30.700
back is straight. Small smile on your
face. Don't crunch up your face,

00:19:30.700 --> 00:19:39.059
don't wrinkle, don't frown. Okay, here we
go.

00:19:39.059 --> 00:19:50.970
The mouth should not be too tight. The
lip should be relaxed. The forehead

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:56.519
should be relaxed. The eyelids should be
relaxed.

00:19:56.519 --> 00:20:13.249
The hands should be relaxed. The back is
straight. The shoulder blades are pushed

00:20:13.249 --> 00:20:23.620
together and your chest comes out a
little bit, which means that your hands

00:20:23.620 --> 00:20:37.919
might come back more on your thighs than
on your knees. It's very good for your

00:20:37.919 --> 00:20:51.679
posture if your lower abdomen is firm,

00:20:51.679 --> 00:20:55.940
but not pulled in with effort.

00:20:55.940 --> 00:21:11.029
So, how to get that firm abdomen which
gives you a strong back? There's a nice

00:21:11.029 --> 00:21:28.350
trick. When you breathe out, and you
finish your out-breath, then consciously

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:36.549
try to push out a little more air from
your lungs and that will tighten your

00:21:36.549 --> 00:21:48.620
lower abdomen. And that will make it
easier to sit up straight. So, let's start

00:21:48.620 --> 00:21:53.190
with ten breaths

00:21:53.190 --> 00:22:05.129
before we start the first of the seven
steps.

00:22:05.129 --> 00:22:18.269
Very slow exhale. At the end of the
exhale press a little more breath out.

00:22:18.269 --> 00:22:27.860
Don't worry about the in-breath, it will
take care of itself. Make sure your lower

00:22:27.860 --> 00:22:40.639
abdomen is tightening slightly at
the end of the out-breath. Pushing out

00:22:40.639 --> 00:22:53.049
the last bit of air from your lungs. It
will also prevent a buildup of prana, or

00:22:53.049 --> 00:23:00.220
lung (RLUNG), or chi; and then you
won't get feelings of nervousness as

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:10.820
you meditate. Small smile. Eyelids are soft.

00:23:10.820 --> 00:24:23.570
Let's do ten long exhales.

00:24:23.570 --> 00:24:31.929
Now we'll start the first of the seven
warm-up steps.

00:24:31.929 --> 00:24:39.559
Invite one of those teachers to come to
sit with you. Could be any of those

00:24:39.559 --> 00:24:54.360
teachers we talked about. Very powerful
person to sak jang with them. Very

00:24:54.360 --> 00:25:03.879
powerful for planting good seeds, very
powerful for cleaning bad seeds.

00:25:03.879 --> 00:25:21.919
And you invite them and they come and
sit in front of you on the same level. I

00:25:21.919 --> 00:25:31.970
like to say knee to knee, and to
understand they are not a statue or a

00:25:31.970 --> 00:25:46.509
painting. It's a real person in front of
me. I can see their chest moving with

00:25:46.509 --> 00:26:04.299
their breath. I can feel the subtle
warmth from their body knee to knee. Good

00:26:04.299 --> 00:26:15.220
people have a certain delicate fragrance
to them. Like a very subtle jasmine

00:26:15.220 --> 00:26:19.539
smell.

00:26:19.539 --> 00:26:27.780
So, get this teacher's image in front of
you. It's not a painting; it's a real

00:26:27.780 --> 00:26:45.649
person. Your eyes are closed, but their
eyes are open. They are looking at you as

00:26:45.649 --> 00:26:58.040
you meditate, and they're very pleased
with you that you are meditating. Just

00:26:58.040 --> 00:27:58.740
enjoy being with them. We're going to
meditate together.

00:27:58.740 --> 00:28:11.570
The second of the seven warm-up steps is
to make an offering to your teacher. And

00:28:11.570 --> 00:28:22.549
it just sets the feeling of the
meditation as very happy. So, imagine any

00:28:22.549 --> 00:28:37.210
beautiful gift. I think Nagarjuna
liked coconut. There's a

00:28:37.210 --> 00:28:47.669
traditional offering to imagine the
whole sky covered with flowers, and make

00:28:47.669 --> 00:29:04.259
this offering. There's a very special
offering to your teacher and that is to

00:29:04.259 --> 00:29:14.389
bow down to that teacher by thinking
about some beautiful quality that they

00:29:14.389 --> 00:29:29.960
have. So, I'm thinking of Arya Nagarjuna.
Good humor, funny person, extremely

00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:42.429
brilliant, and knows how to write
beautiful, beautiful short things. So I'll

00:29:42.429 --> 00:30:13.169
just appreciate Nagarjuna. And that's a high
offering. You appreciate your own

00:30:13.169 --> 00:30:22.649
teacher.

00:30:22.649 --> 00:30:48.070
The third of the seven preparation steps

00:30:48.070 --> 00:30:59.950
is to clean away the bad seeds you've
made in the last 24 hours. So, spend a few

00:30:59.950 --> 00:31:11.809
minutes to open your heart. Let your
teacher look inside, and show them the

00:31:11.809 --> 00:31:17.570
mistakes you have made in the last 24
hours.

00:31:17.570 --> 00:31:31.289
Don't be shy. Be completely honest. And
that kind of willingness to show your

00:31:31.289 --> 00:31:46.799
teacher your mistakes, and to promise
them you'll try harder today, this kills

00:31:46.799 --> 00:32:04.190
those old bad seeds. And that will make
your meditation much sweeter.

00:32:04.190 --> 00:32:16.029
Personally I like to spend ten breaths on
each of the seven steps. Sometimes twenty if

00:32:16.029 --> 00:32:44.429
my mind is kind of busy.

00:32:44.429 --> 00:33:17.320
Okay, now preparation step number four.

00:33:17.320 --> 00:33:29.519
We're going to balance thinking about the
bad seeds by thinking about some good

00:33:29.519 --> 00:33:45.159
things we did. It's very much human
nature to focus on our mistakes, and we

00:33:45.159 --> 00:33:59.989
don't give equal time to the good things
we did. So, now ten relaxed breaths thinking

00:33:59.989 --> 00:34:10.250
about the sweetest things you did, mostly
for other people, in the last 24 hours.

00:34:10.250 --> 00:34:18.610
You can include your meditation
time as something you're happy about.

00:34:18.610 --> 00:34:30.351
Okay, here we go.
Ten breaths. What are some of the sweet

00:34:30.351 --> 00:34:48.480
things you did in the last 24 hours

00:34:48.480 --> 00:35:13.520
for other people?

00:35:13.520 --> 00:35:47.940
And now we're ready for the fifth of the
seven preparation steps. And in our mind

00:35:47.940 --> 00:35:57.870
we ask our teacher to continue teaching
us. Remember that the teachers teaching

00:35:57.870 --> 00:36:09.520
can come to us in many ways.
Oh sure, sometimes we get a video talking

00:36:09.520 --> 00:36:23.260
about the steps to the path. Maybe we
read a scripture. Maybe we go to listen

00:36:23.260 --> 00:36:36.610
to a teacher in person. But negative
things also teach us a lot. The

00:36:36.610 --> 00:36:48.470
challenges and disappointments in our
life, they often teach us more than the

00:36:48.470 --> 00:37:02.510
successes. So, here in this fifth step it
can be a kind of surrender. "Oh, teacher

00:37:02.510 --> 00:37:13.710
please teach me, let good teachings come
to me and let difficult teachings come

00:37:13.710 --> 00:37:26.040
to me, and I will have courage." "I will be
strong, and I will also learn from the

00:37:26.040 --> 00:37:44.161
difficult parts of my life; so I trust
you." "Send me sweet dharma teachings, but

00:37:44.161 --> 00:37:56.250
please also send me difficult teachings—
problems in my life—like very

00:37:56.250 --> 00:38:04.330
challenging viruses, and I will do my
best to become a better person from

00:38:04.330 --> 00:38:14.680
these challenges."

00:38:14.680 --> 00:38:19.270
Then when difficult situations come to
you, please remember you asked your

00:38:19.270 --> 00:38:39.460
teacher to send them. And don't get
discouraged and don't get off balance;

00:38:39.460 --> 00:38:48.660
use them to become stronger. When
difficult times come to you, use it as a

00:38:48.660 --> 00:39:06.390
reason to serve more people. This virus
is an excellent time for Buddhists. This

00:39:06.390 --> 00:39:18.300
is a great opportunity to show other
people what is a Buddhist. The more

00:39:18.300 --> 00:39:27.440
dangerous life is, the more financial
trouble we have, the more doubts and

00:39:27.440 --> 00:39:37.590
fears that people have—a real Buddhist
person steps up—this is their time to

00:39:37.590 --> 00:39:50.830
show how much they can help people.

00:39:50.830 --> 00:39:54.990
If a Buddhist person has a face mask
and another person does not have a face

00:39:54.990 --> 00:40:09.920
mask, the Buddhist person happily gives
the face mask to the other person. And

00:40:09.920 --> 00:41:05.450
we're happy we had the chance to do it.

00:41:05.450 --> 00:41:27.681
The sixth preparation step is to ask
this teacher to stay in our life. Ask

00:41:27.681 --> 00:41:38.080
them not to leave our life. The karma—
the good seeds to have a teacher—they

00:41:38.080 --> 00:41:58.920
are perhaps the most rare seeds in the
world, and may I always plant those seeds

00:41:58.920 --> 00:42:44.390
to have you in my life. Please stay in my
life.

00:42:44.390 --> 00:42:53.560
The seventh step in the meditation, the

00:42:53.560 --> 00:43:04.540
last one, it comes after the actual
meditation. So, you do these six steps

00:43:04.540 --> 00:43:12.730
that we just did, then you do your actual
meditation, which might be one of the

00:43:12.730 --> 00:43:27.400
steps of the path. Like a death
meditation, or an emptiness meditation, or

00:43:27.400 --> 00:43:37.120
a tong len (GTONG LEN)—"giving and
taking"—meditation, or exchanging myself

00:43:37.120 --> 00:43:46.950
and others. And then after you finish the
meditation, you think about all the good

00:43:46.950 --> 00:43:56.290
seeds you planted by doing the
meditation, and then you very consciously

00:43:56.290 --> 00:44:06.900
put them in the bank. When you dedicate
any good seed to another person's

00:44:06.900 --> 00:44:19.180
happiness, then that seed is protected
and it will always stay with you. So,

00:44:19.180 --> 00:44:27.820
paradoxically you keep the seed by
giving it away.

00:44:27.820 --> 00:44:47.310
So, the seventh step of meditation. After
your main meditation is completed, then

00:44:47.310 --> 00:44:55.540
imagine that you are sharing the good
seeds you planted by meditating. And you

00:44:55.540 --> 00:45:04.580
are sending them out to all the people
in this world. Start with people who are

00:45:04.580 --> 00:45:14.010
in the same room. Then share those good
seeds with other people in your

00:45:14.010 --> 00:45:26.770
neighborhood. Then send the seeds to
all the people in your city, and share

00:45:26.770 --> 00:45:37.820
them with everyone in your country. Then
share them with everyone in this planet,

00:45:37.820 --> 00:45:40.920
and then send them out to outer space—to
share with all the people living in

00:45:40.920 --> 00:45:49.240
other worlds. There's a tradition to do
this

00:45:49.240 --> 00:46:00.800
sharing of the good seeds of our
meditation, by imagining those seeds as a

00:46:00.800 --> 00:46:13.250
golden light. And at the end of our
meditation we will take at least three

00:46:13.250 --> 00:46:25.790
very, very slow deep exhales, and we will
send those good seeds out. Share them

00:46:25.790 --> 00:46:31.930
with other people as a beautiful golden
light.

00:46:31.930 --> 00:47:15.520
Okay, let's do it together.

00:47:15.520 --> 00:47:21.570
One last suggestion about your
meditation, and then we're finished with

00:47:21.570 --> 00:47:33.030
this segment and this month's
practice. So, I've been meditating for

00:47:33.030 --> 00:47:45.040
over 40 years, but there have been
periods in my life when I became

00:47:45.040 --> 00:47:54.330
busy. Maybe I was too busy teaching
meditation and I didn't have time to do

00:47:54.330 --> 00:48:00.560
my own meditation. And I just want to tell
you that this will happen to every

00:48:00.560 --> 00:48:15.160
meditator, and then don't get very
disturbed. When you're ready, start your

00:48:15.160 --> 00:48:26.261
meditations again. And what I've learned
after many years of meditating, start

00:48:26.261 --> 00:48:38.190
with the very short meditations. 15
minutes, 20 minutes; start back or begin

00:48:38.190 --> 00:48:51.260
meditation with short ones. Then once a
week increase those meditations by just

00:48:51.260 --> 00:49:03.850
one minute. So, this week 15 minutes. Every
day.

00:49:03.850 --> 00:49:15.910
Same time is helpful, then on Sunday
increase to 16 minutes. And the next

00:49:15.910 --> 00:49:27.320
Sunday increase to 17 minutes.
And in this way, within half a year, you

00:49:27.320 --> 00:49:36.450
will have a very good 40-50 minutes of
meditation. And within a year, you'll have

00:49:36.450 --> 00:49:46.600
a very good 1 hour of meditation. And
that's our goal; to have one hour of

00:49:46.600 --> 00:49:57.400
meditation per day. To build up to one
hour, which is perfect for seeing

00:49:57.400 --> 00:50:13.480
emptiness. Slowly open your eyes. Take a
good stretch. Thank you Alison for

00:50:13.480 --> 00:50:16.340
translating, and see you guys in segment 3.

